today's video is all about wands in Enel  crossing new horizons and everything you  need to know about them wizard what do  they do how can you get them and how  many kinds are there let's go ahead and  jump into it right now people of the  internet retro raconteur here and  welcome back to another animal crossing  new horizons video one of my favourite  items in the game has to be the wand or  wands plural as there are quite a few of  them here's a quick look at all the  different types of ones you can get in  Animal Crossing new horizons and here in  a bit we're gonna go through each wand  and I'll show you exactly how they're  obtained if you don't have a one yet and  you're unsure what they do it's pretty  straightforward wands are simply a tool  for quickly changing outfits anytime  anywhere if you're new to the game you  may have found out about once through a  DIY recipe or perhaps you saw someone  else using one I actually found out by  getting multiple DIY recipes before I  ever knew their actual function in the  game  wands can be equipped like any other  tools such as a shovel or fishing rod  the purpose of the wand though is to  quickly alter your appearance without  having to access a wardrobe item or  going into your inventory to swap out  different pieces of your outfit so even  though there are different types of  wands in the game they all have the same  purpose so how do you go about obtaining  these wands there are two steps you'll  need to complete to make your own one  and you're about to see why it's been so  hard for me to get those recipes first  you'll have to get the correct recipe  second you'll need to find the  appropriate crafting items now most of  the recipes are obtained from celeste so  make sure you talk to her anytime you  see her visiting and she'll always have  a recipe for you unfortunately the  recipes from celeste won't always be  wand recipes now there are also certain  wands tied to special events in the game  there's the bug wand and fish wand which  are both obtained as rewards from their  respective events ie the bug off and  fishing tournament the bunny day wand  was obtained after completing the entire  bunny day series of furniture for zipper  cherry blossom wand is from the cherry  blossom festival you'll have a chance at  the ice wand DIY recipe for making  perfect snow boys during winter time the  mushroom wand can be obtained tearing  you guessed it mushrooming season  there's also the wedding wand which is a  recipe you can get from Syrus after  completing seven days of photo shoots  during wedding season and finally  there's the shell wand which you  obtain from your regular DIY recipe  sources now all the other Wan recipes I  haven't mentioned so far are obtained  from Celeste so here we go the cosmos  golden hyacinth iron lily pansy rose  star tree branch tulip wand and the wind  flower are all wand recipes you'll need  to get from Celeste or trading with a  friend of course so if you have your  sights set on a particular one now you  know how to get the recipe but that's  only half the battle you see one recipes  do require star fragments which is  somewhat of a rare item in the game the  only way to get them is by wishing on a  star during meteor showers the star  fragments will then wash on your Shore  throughout the next day  make sure you wish on as many shooting  stars as you can and also check the  beach a couple of times over the course  of the next day as the star fragments  will continue to appear if you're having  a hard time catching a meteor shower  then you may want to check out media  nook a free online tool that will show  you the exact day and time you need to  be on the lookout for shooting stars I  made a whole separate video on media  nuke as there is quite a bit of setup  involved and I'll be sure to include a  link to that down in the description  below ok so you got your recipe you  crafted your wand now how do you  actually use the thing before you can  use the wand you'll want to create a few  different outfit combinations you can  make up to eight and you'll need to do  so from any wardrobe style item even  items like coolers and refrigerators  will work strange I know it's pretty  straightforward to set them up from  there but unfortunately there are a few  strange limitations first if you have  any items you'd like to use across  multiple outfits say a specific pair of  socks a hat you love or your beard yes  for some reason beers or cosmetic items  in this game I don't get it it makes me  mad I I have a beard but if that's the  case then you'll only be able to use  that item on one outfit if you want to  use it in more than one unfortunately  you'll need to buy multiple versions of  the item yeah you got it that means I  have to buy multiple beards you also  can't set your wet suit as a wand outfit  but you can easily get around this by  starting off wearing your wet suit and  then using your wand to change into your  preloaded outfits any time you want to  switch back to the wet suit you simply  remove your current outfit with your  wand  another small downside is you won't be  able to enter the changing room at the a  sister shop while wearing either a star  outfit or your wet suit even with those  limitations though wands are a fantastic  fun addition to the game especially if  you have multiple outfits you like to  wear and come on this is animal crossing  who doesn't have multiple outfits they  want to wear I'm hopeful the down the  line will see a Nintendo iron out some  of those minor issues to make them even  better you should now be seeing two  videos popping up on the right side of  your screen one is all about setting up  the media Nook site so you can predict  your weather and meteor showers the  other is about that little trick I  mentioned regarding your wand and  wetsuit that's gonna be it for this  video I'll talk to you guys again soon
 

